The length yajl gives is a size_t

yajl_gen_get_buf() writes the length of its buffer through a size_t pointer.
The handler gives it the address of an unsigned int: the same on 32-bit ARM,
and on a 64-bit machine neither accepted by the compiler nor right, since
eight bytes would be written into four.

